License: GPL-3.0-only.

Modified 2026-11-05: Python streaming upload; local 10-minute segmentation;
whole-source timestamp restoration; retained raw responses and task records;
three-parameter standalone/Tiance JSON entry; explicit error handling;
unified media inspection, decoding, trimming and encoding through PyAV.
Long recordings are evenly partitioned below ten minutes per part, processed
with up to 20 concurrent cloud tasks, and merged in original timeline order.
Supported AAC-LC/MP4 tracks retain compressed packets with frame-aligned cuts
and MP4 edit lists. Other layouts retain decoded FLAC extraction. Atomic result
writes retry transient Windows file sharing errors within the job budget.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses and notices. The tool
bundles an audio-focused PyAV 16.0.1+audio.1 build for Windows x64 CPython 3.13,
linked to FFmpeg 8.0.1 shared libraries and zlib 1.3.1. Sources, hashes and the
build recipe are documented in native-build/. PyAV's only source modification
is its local version in av/about.py; delvewheel adjusts DLL loading and names.
FFmpeg and zlib sources are unmodified. Optional video codecs, external codec
libraries, devices and networking are disabled in this FFmpeg configuration.

PyAV: BSD-3-Clause; FFmpeg: LGPL-2.1-or-later; zlib: zlib license.
License texts are in program/vendor/cp313-win_amd64/
av-16.0.1+audio.1.dist-info/licenses/. These shared libraries can be replaced or
rebuilt independently; the tool does not enforce signatures on replacements.
No imageio-ffmpeg distribution or separate ffmpeg executable is bundled.
